<%# A reviewer's feedback as the builder reads it on their timeline: prose
    first, then whatever the reviewer asked for as a bullet list.

    Read-only counterpart to projects/_action_items, which renders the same asks
    as boxes to tick on the resubmit form. Both go through
    Certification::Reviewable, so the "- do the thing" syntax a reviewer types
    is only ever parsed in one place - and never shown to the builder raw.

    Locals: review - a Certification::Reviewable carrying feedback. %>
<div class="review-feedback">
  <% if review.feedback_prose.present? %>
    <div class="review-feedback__prose"><%= simple_format(review.feedback_prose, {}, sanitize: true) %></div>
  <% end %>

  <% if review.action_items.any? %>
    <ul class="review-feedback__items">
      <% review.action_items.each do |item| %>
        <li class="review-feedback__item"><%= item %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  <% end %>
</div>
